# Wave W17-AC (Route 228): wash turf — dry-wash green, dust flecks: a dusty olive green the washes wander onto, carrying pale dust flecks blown off the sand country it islands in (design: the sand country — the road gives up at the storm fence, the green gives up sooner, in washes). The shipped sand family stands byte-identical entire around it (Ruling #3 — the sand IS the route’s identity); this turf is the island, not the sea. Route 228’s own ground — split from its twin Route 111 (Maris) by geography entire (a plateau island of washes ending at a fence vs grass failing into dunes) and from Route 226’s cliff turf by dryness: dust flecks here, spray flecks there.
